---
import LifecycleIcon from "../icons/LifecycleIcon.astro";
import IdentityIcon from "../icons/IdentityIcon.astro";
import LockIcon from "../icons/LockIcon.astro";
import AuditIcon from "../icons/AuditIcon.astro";
---

<!--
  Governed async tasks. Available from core 2.0.0.

  Written for someone deciding whether they need this, not for someone
  reviewing the implementation. Earlier revisions led with internals (the
  store type, the ledger key, JSON-RPC error codes) and with the history of
  how the wire got here -- answers to a question nobody arrives with.

  Keep: the gap being closed, the shape of the lifecycle, one concrete
  scenario, and what you can answer afterwards that you could not before.
  Deliberately absent: ADR links, issue numbers, SDK-vendoring history, and
  "not in 1.x" framing -- 1.x is closed, so its absence is not news.
-->
<section id="async-governance" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-32">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <div
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/30 text-emerald-300 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider cursor-default mb-5"
            role="status"
        >
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400" aria-hidden="true"/>
            Available from 2.0.0
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
            Governed async tasks
        </h2>
        <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-100">
            Your longest-running operations were the least governed ones
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-zinc-400 max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-4">
            A synchronous tool call is decided while it happens. An async one hands back a
            handle in milliseconds and does the real work later &mdash; the export, the
            migration, the bulk write. Everything expensive and hard to undo lives there,
            and it is exactly the shape that slips past a policy engine watching the request.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The schematic: who asks, where Hangar interposes, what it does there. -->
    <div class="mb-6 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-900/30 border border-zinc-800/50">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-6 text-center">
            Where Hangar sits in a task&rsquo;s life
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <div class="min-w-[640px] grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr_auto_1fr] items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-4">
                <div class="text-center text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">Your client</div>
                <div aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div class="text-center text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80">Hangar</div>
                <div aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div class="text-center text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">MCP server</div>

                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50 text-center">
                    <p class="text-zinc-200 text-sm font-medium">Calls a slow tool</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-zinc-600 text-lg text-center" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/[0.07] border border-emerald-500/25 text-center">
                    <p class="text-emerald-200 text-sm font-medium">Records the task</p>
                    <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-1">before the handle is handed back</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-zinc-600 text-lg text-center" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50 text-center">
                    <p class="text-zinc-200 text-sm font-medium">Starts the work</p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50 text-center">
                    <p class="text-zinc-200 text-sm font-medium">Answers a question</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-zinc-600 text-lg text-center" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/[0.07] border border-emerald-500/25 text-center">
                    <p class="text-emerald-200 text-sm font-medium">Consent gate</p>
                    <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-1">the answer passes policy first</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-zinc-600 text-lg text-center" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50 text-center">
                    <p class="text-zinc-200 text-sm font-medium">Pauses, then resumes</p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50 text-center">
                    <p class="text-zinc-200 text-sm font-medium">Collects the result</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-zinc-600 text-lg text-center" aria-hidden="true">&larr;</div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/[0.07] border border-emerald-500/25 text-center">
                    <p class="text-emerald-200 text-sm font-medium">Re-checks the tool</p>
                    <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-1">drift fails the task, not silently</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-zinc-600 text-lg text-center" aria-hidden="true">&larr;</div>
                <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50 text-center">
                    <p class="text-zinc-200 text-sm font-medium">Finishes</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs text-center mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            Hangar relays; it never becomes the executor. No scheduler, no job runner, no
            result store of its own &mdash; the work stays where it was, and only the
            decisions move.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- One concrete scenario, told as a before/after. -->
    <div class="mb-6 p-6 md:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-900/30 border border-zinc-800/50">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400">
                <LifecycleIcon />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">What this looks like in practice</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm mb-5 max-w-3xl">
            An agent asks your warehouse server to export a customer dataset. The export takes
            twenty minutes, so the server returns a handle immediately. Half a minute in, it
            needs a decision: <em>include the columns holding personal data?</em>
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/40 border border-zinc-800/50">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500 mb-3">Ungoverned</p>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">
                    <li>The agent answers the question itself. Nothing evaluates that answer.</li>
                    <li>The export runs with whatever it decided.</li>
                    <li>Your audit trail holds one line: a call was made, and a handle came back.</li>
                    <li>Asked later who authorised personal data leaving, you cannot say.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/[0.04] border border-emerald-500/20">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80 mb-3">With Hangar</p>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-300">
                    <li>The handle is recorded before the agent ever sees it.</li>
                    <li>The answer crosses the consent gate before it reaches the server.</li>
                    <li>If the tool&rsquo;s schema changed mid-flight, the result is refused rather than delivered.</li>
                    <li>The whole sequence &mdash; who, what, when, which tenant &mdash; replays from the event stream.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What you can answer afterwards that you could not before. -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-900/30 border border-zinc-800/50">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 mb-4">
                <LockIcon />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100 mb-2">No orphaned handles</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm">
                Every task Hangar relays is one it knows about, so a follow-up always resolves.
                A task belonging to another tenant is refused exactly the way one that never
                existed is &mdash; you cannot probe for what you do not own.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-900/30 border border-zinc-800/50">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 mb-4">
                <IdentityIcon />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100 mb-2">The pause is a checkpoint</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm">
                When a task stops to ask something, the question and its answer are governed
                like any other call &mdash; not waved through because the work already started.
                A failed relay leaves the decision unspent, so a retry is a retry and not a
                second authorisation.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-900/30 border border-zinc-800/50">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 mb-4">
                <AuditIcon />
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-100 mb-2">A chain that survives the wait</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm">
                Creation, every decision, and the outcome are appended as they happen, keyed to
                the task and carrying tenant and correlation. Twenty minutes later the record is
                still a sequence, not an inference.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-center text-sm text-zinc-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Nothing here prompts a human. There is no inbox and no &ldquo;click to allow&rdquo;
        &mdash; decisions come from policy and from the client driving the exchange, which is
        what keeps an unattended agent unattended.
        <a href="/docs/guides/GOVERNED_TASKS" class="text-zinc-400 underline decoration-zinc-600 hover:decoration-zinc-400">How it works</a>.
    </p>
</section>
